WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today

2
00:00:23.125 --> 00:00:25.684
<i>All of us have a list in our lives.</i>

3
00:00:25.708 --> 00:00:28.226
<i>A list of dreams and simple joys.</i>

4
00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:31.583
<i>My list has always been filled with
new journeys and new places.</i>

5
00:00:32.083 --> 00:00:35.875
<i>I'm Preeti. and one journey on my list
led me to Musafir Cafe.</i>

6
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.393
<i>What is Musafir Cafe?</i>

7
00:00:38.417 --> 00:00:41.518
<i>Ask anyone. and you'll hear
a different answer every time.</i>

8
00:00:41.542 --> 00:00:45.083
<i>To me. it's home.
Chander's and mine.</i>

9
00:00:47.125 --> 00:00:50.792
<i>Your dark. beautiful eyes.</i>

10
00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:54.042
<i>Looked up and met mine.</i>

11
00:00:54.625 --> 00:00:59.333
<i>The flowing breeze. the passing scenes.</i>

12
00:01:00.125 --> 00:01:01.750
<i>Everything stood still.</i>

13
00:01:02.542 --> 00:01:03.768
Hey! Hi!

14
00:01:03.792 --> 00:01:05.792
Wait. one second.

15
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:08.476
-Hi!
-You guys are coming tonight. right?

16
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.059
No.

17
00:01:10.083 --> 00:01:13.893
I can't believe Rajvir planned a trek
with his friends today.

18
00:01:13.917 --> 00:01:16.167
and now I'll miss tonight's party.

19
00:01:16.792 --> 00:01:19.976
Well. I have a feeling
you're really going to love this trek!

20
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.500
-Is it?
-Yeah! Have a great time. you two!

21
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.018
Okay. Bye.

22
00:01:24.042 --> 00:01:25.208
Bye!

23
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.434
<i>What kind of magic.</i>

24
00:01:30.458 --> 00:01:33.101
<i>Have you cast on me?</i>

25
00:01:33.125 --> 00:01:34.750
<i>Tell me. haven't you?</i>

26
00:01:38.875 --> 00:01:43.809
<i>Stars fell like jasmine blossoms
Upon my rooftop...</i>

27
00:01:43.833 --> 00:01:47.059
<i>For every traveler.
the journey truly begins</i>

28
00:01:47.083 --> 00:01:49.375
<i>when they find their true companion.</i>

29
00:01:50.958 --> 00:01:53.226
<i>Sometimes. that companion
stays by their side.</i>

30
00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:55.720
<i>And. sometimes. they leave
after changing you forever.</i>

31
00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:09.601
<i>What kind of magic.</i>

32
00:02:09.625 --> 00:02:12.268
<i>Have you cast on me?</i>

33
00:02:12.292 --> 00:02:14.226
<i>Tell me. haven't you?</i>

34
00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:17.809
<i>Something similar happened to me
when I met Chander.</i>

35
00:02:17.833 --> 00:02:21.458
<i>And. perhaps. his life changed
in much the same way</i>

36
00:02:21.958 --> 00:02:23.208
<i>when he met Sudha.</i>

37
00:02:53.292 --> 00:02:56.268
Mom. tilt the phone down a bit.
You're not in the frame.

38
00:02:56.292 --> 00:02:57.768
<i>-Is this okay?</i>
-Yes. I can see you now.

39
00:02:57.792 --> 00:02:59.667
{\an8}<i>-Have you arrived?</i>
-Yes. I'm here.

40
00:03:00.167 --> 00:03:01.351
{\an8}Early. as usual.

41
00:03:01.375 --> 00:03:02.726
{\an8}<i>Did you pick a good place?</i>

42
00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:06.309
{\an8}-She picked it. Look how pretty it is.
<i>-Yes. it's beautiful.</i>

43
00:03:06.333 --> 00:03:08.143
{\an8}I didn't even know about this place.

44
00:03:08.167 --> 00:03:09.333
{\an8}<i>How would you know?</i>

45
00:03:09.958 --> 00:03:12.125
{\an8}<i>-You're always busy with work!</i>
-Mom...

46
00:03:12.708 --> 00:03:15.583
{\an8}-Should I hang up now?
<i>-Wait. just a minute.</i>

47
00:03:16.208 --> 00:03:17.351
{\an8}<i>Thank you.</i>

48
00:03:17.375 --> 00:03:20.208
{\an8}<i>-I know that in your heart. you still...</i>
-Mom.

49
00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.917
Please don't start this again.

50
00:03:23.625 --> 00:03:25.101
<i>-Okay. fine.</i>
-I'm hanging up.

51
00:03:25.125 --> 00:03:26.708
She'll be here any minute. Bye.

52
00:03:34.875 --> 00:03:37.059
-Where's your coffee from?
-From the South. sir.

53
00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:41.167
What do you mean by South? Tamil Nadu?
Karnataka? Kerala? Where exactly?

54
00:03:41.664 --> 00:03:44.809
-Sir. that's...
-Is it blended or single origin?

55
00:03:44.833 --> 00:03:48.792
-Sir...
-Okay. is the grind medium or medium-fine?

56
00:03:49.583 --> 00:03:50.434
It's medium-fine. sir.

57
00:03:50.458 --> 00:03:52.018
I know that for sure. it's medium-fine.

58
00:03:52.042 --> 00:03:53.143
-Are you sure?
-Yes. sir.

59
00:03:53.167 --> 00:03:54.934
Then do one thing. Mohan.

60
00:03:54.958 --> 00:03:56.226
Some coffee.

61
00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:59.726
some hot water between
90 and 95 degrees Celsius.

62
00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:03.417
an empty pot. and an Americano cup.
Please bring all of this.

63
00:04:04.208 --> 00:04:07.559
-Sir. are you sure the machine coffee...
-No. that won't work.

64
00:04:07.583 --> 00:04:11.809
Don't worry. I'll pay the full amount.
and I'll tip you too.

65
00:04:11.833 --> 00:04:13.792
Okay. sir. I'll bring it.

66
00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.893
Excuse me!
What do you software engineers think?

67
00:04:20.917 --> 00:04:22.976
Is moving to America a career now?

68
00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.809
No. no. It's just for two years.

69
00:04:25.833 --> 00:04:27.726
So. you'll go to America for two years.

70
00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:30.268
and I'm supposed to leave
my practice and follow you?

71
00:04:30.292 --> 00:04:32.000
-How will I live alone?
-Live alone?!

72
00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:34.726
Take your mom with you
to take care of you!

73
00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:36.667
Why do you need to get married?

74
00:04:37.542 --> 00:04:39.208
The nerve of some people!

75
00:04:42.417 --> 00:04:45.893
Hello. I just wanted to let you know
that I've arrived.

76
00:04:45.917 --> 00:04:47.250
Yes. I'm coming!

77
00:04:48.125 --> 00:04:49.101
What are you looking at?

78
00:04:49.125 --> 00:04:51.743
Are you leaving. or do you
need a green card for that too?

79
00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:55.500
How about I roll out a red carpet for you?
Get lost!

80
00:05:06.875 --> 00:05:07.875
Hi.

81
00:05:08.542 --> 00:05:09.875
Sorry to keep you waiting.

82
00:05:11.042 --> 00:05:12.167
I'm Sudha.

83
00:05:15.292 --> 00:05:16.542
You spoke very well.

84
00:05:17.833 --> 00:05:18.833
I'm Chander.

85
00:05:19.458 --> 00:05:20.726
Were you eavesdropping?

86
00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:23.726
I wasn't eavesdropping.
I could just hear you.

87
00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:25.042
Everyone could.

88
00:05:26.917 --> 00:05:28.708
-Shall we sit?
-Please.

89
00:05:35.333 --> 00:05:37.893
-Can you bring another cup of tea. Mohan?
-Yeah.

90
00:05:37.917 --> 00:05:39.000
The usual.

91
00:05:44.042 --> 00:05:46.083
Sorry. just give me a minute. please.

92
00:06:03.292 --> 00:06:07.292
You came here to make your own coffee?

93
00:06:09.167 --> 00:06:11.042
I'm a bit particular about my coffee.

94
00:06:12.708 --> 00:06:15.208
Nice cafe. by the way.
Do you come here often?

95
00:06:15.792 --> 00:06:17.101
But I don't drink coffee.

96
00:06:17.125 --> 00:06:18.268
I'm a chai lover.

97
00:06:18.292 --> 00:06:19.417
Chai!

98
00:06:20.417 --> 00:06:22.726
And along with my Sunday tea.

99
00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:25.917
I also get samples
from matrimonial sites. Free!

100
00:06:29.792 --> 00:06:33.042
Who made your profile?
Your mom or your dad?

101
00:06:35.208 --> 00:06:37.476
{\an8}Excuse me. Oh. man.

102
00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:38.792
{\an8}MOM:
HAS SHE ARRIVED? HOW IS SHE?

103
00:06:43.625 --> 00:06:45.750
If you don't mind.
can I ask you something?

104
00:06:46.917 --> 00:06:49.059
Do you have another candidate
lined up after me?

105
00:06:49.083 --> 00:06:52.917
No. If there is. I'll wrap up accordingly.

106
00:06:53.917 --> 00:06:55.667
So. we don't overlap again.

107
00:06:56.792 --> 00:06:59.250
So. you're a lawyer?

108
00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.000
Yes.

109
00:07:02.097 --> 00:07:03.097
Divorce lawyer.

110
00:07:04.667 --> 00:07:06.393
My family usually hides that part.

111
00:07:06.417 --> 00:07:07.857
It frightens the suitor's side away.

112
00:07:09.083 --> 00:07:10.417
But I love my job.

113
00:07:11.917 --> 00:07:14.167
So. you enjoy getting people divorced?

114
00:07:14.958 --> 00:07:15.958
No.

115
00:07:16.625 --> 00:07:17.809
To be honest.

116
00:07:17.833 --> 00:07:20.750
the divorce happens
long before it reaches the courtroom.

117
00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:22.458
We just help them

118
00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:25.167
get the official stamp and...

119
00:07:25.958 --> 00:07:27.792
settle the accounts.

120
00:07:30.667 --> 00:07:31.667
Ma'am.

121
00:07:32.292 --> 00:07:33.458
Thanks. Mohan.

122
00:07:37.125 --> 00:07:40.083
You handle divorce cases.
and you still want to get married?

123
00:07:42.208 --> 00:07:44.250
Well. about that...

124
00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:48.250
I don't want to get married right now.

125
00:07:49.042 --> 00:07:52.434
I meet suitors to stop my relatives
from pestering my mom.

126
00:07:52.458 --> 00:07:55.292
I always find an excuse to reject them.

127
00:07:58.208 --> 00:08:00.851
You should reject software engineers
without even meeting them.

128
00:08:00.875 --> 00:08:03.750
-Aren't you a software engineer too?
-I was.

129
00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:05.500
I got bored.

130
00:08:06.125 --> 00:08:08.434
I work at DWD Logistics now.

131
00:08:08.458 --> 00:08:10.500
I'm setting up their MP operations.

132
00:08:11.375 --> 00:08:14.268
-Why did you choose that job?
-It's far from my family.

133
00:08:14.292 --> 00:08:15.625
From Delhi. that's why.

134
00:08:16.250 --> 00:08:17.833
And from your ex-girlfriend too.

135
00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:22.625
-No. No.
-No?

136
00:08:23.125 --> 00:08:25.167
No. it's nothing like that.

137
00:08:25.833 --> 00:08:27.292
You're just assuming that.

138
00:08:28.458 --> 00:08:30.851
Just one of the small perks
of being a lawyer.

139
00:08:30.875 --> 00:08:33.625
I've learned how to read people's faces.

140
00:08:34.917 --> 00:08:36.958
Don't you find logistics boring?

141
00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:40.417
A little less than life itself.

142
00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:49.726
So. how are you spending
the rest of your Sunday?

143
00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:53.559
My plan was to meet you and then
head to the theater to watch a movie.

144
00:08:53.583 --> 00:08:55.750
There's so much to do in Bhopal.

145
00:08:56.333 --> 00:08:58.813
yet you want to sit in the dark
and watch someone else's story?

146
00:09:00.625 --> 00:09:03.083
Okay then. tell me.
what would you recommend?

147
00:09:03.667 --> 00:09:07.434
Visit Manav Sangrahalaya.
Take a long walk through Van Vihar.

148
00:09:07.458 --> 00:09:11.976
Or best of all.
enjoy a refreshing lemon soda by the lake.

149
00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:14.083
Feel the heart of Bhopal.

150
00:09:47.750 --> 00:09:49.458
-Shall we?
-Where?

151
00:09:49.958 --> 00:09:53.000
You're the one who said
there's so much to do in Bhopal.

152
00:09:56.750 --> 00:09:58.167
Why did you leave America?

153
00:09:58.708 --> 00:09:59.875
My heart wasn't in it.

154
00:10:00.875 --> 00:10:04.917
Despite the crowds.
there's a strange emptiness there.

155
00:10:07.167 --> 00:10:09.125
I made a few friends at the university.

156
00:10:10.375 --> 00:10:13.458
Learned a little about myself.
and time taught me the rest.

157
00:10:15.167 --> 00:10:17.375
Tell me one thing you learned there.

158
00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:27.500
No matter what happens in life.
you should never forget your roots.

159
00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:30.458
-And...
-And?

160
00:10:33.042 --> 00:10:37.208
And no matter how good the cafe is.
you should make your own coffee.

161
00:10:39.417 --> 00:10:41.351
When you get bored with logistics.

162
00:10:41.375 --> 00:10:43.917
you should set up your own cafe.

163
00:10:52.042 --> 00:10:54.559
Mom visits from Ratlam
once every two months.

164
00:10:54.583 --> 00:10:58.143
Gargi is hardly just my roommate.
She's basically her undercover reporter.

165
00:10:58.167 --> 00:10:59.309
What do you mean?

166
00:10:59.333 --> 00:11:01.167
She's my mom's spy.

167
00:11:04.167 --> 00:11:08.393
By the way. your strategy
to extend the date was pretty smart.

168
00:11:08.417 --> 00:11:11.518
Thank you.
But it wasn't a strategy.

169
00:11:11.542 --> 00:11:12.518
-No?
-No.

170
00:11:12.542 --> 00:11:14.559
I was just following my intuition.

171
00:11:14.583 --> 00:11:16.083
Well. cheers.

172
00:11:16.625 --> 00:11:17.708
Cheers.

173
00:11:26.042 --> 00:11:26.893
Shit.

174
00:11:26.917 --> 00:11:30.101
Chander. I have to go back to the cafe.

175
00:11:30.125 --> 00:11:32.684
Why?
What happened? Did you forget something?

176
00:11:32.708 --> 00:11:33.833
Candidate number three!

177
00:11:34.458 --> 00:11:35.601
-What?
-Chander.

178
00:11:35.625 --> 00:11:37.976
Make an excuse and reject me. okay?

179
00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:39.226
-Hey!
-Thank you.

180
00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:40.250
Why me?

181
00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:45.083
When a girl rejects a guy.
his mother takes it even harder. you know?

182
00:11:45.667 --> 00:11:46.667
Hey!

183
00:11:48.333 --> 00:11:49.667
What even are you?

184
00:12:09.333 --> 00:12:10.875
-Hi.
-Hello.

185
00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:25.393
Want to know
what I wrote on the promise note?

186
00:12:25.417 --> 00:12:26.417
Sure.

187
00:12:27.625 --> 00:12:29.018
You don't have to tell me.

188
00:12:29.042 --> 00:12:31.792
But if you still want to.
I'm good with secrets.

189
00:12:33.417 --> 00:12:37.833
"No matter what happens. this year
I'm going to be brave and take risks."

190
00:12:38.458 --> 00:12:41.143
This is my first note on the promise wall.

191
00:12:41.167 --> 00:12:43.083
I'm sure it won't be the last.

192
00:12:44.542 --> 00:12:48.559
{\an8}<i>Every traveler needs a place
where they can pause for a while.</i>

193
00:12:48.583 --> 00:12:51.518
<i>where they can remember the promises
they've made to themselves.</i>

194
00:12:51.542 --> 00:12:54.083
<i>For many travelers.
this cafe becomes that place.</i>

195
00:12:54.625 --> 00:12:58.750
<i>Maybe that's why they carry a part of it
with them when they leave.</i>

196
00:12:59.333 --> 00:13:01.375
<i>while leaving a part of themselves here.</i>

197
00:13:02.417 --> 00:13:03.417
Hey.

198
00:13:04.208 --> 00:13:05.625
Hey! Hi!

199
00:13:08.833 --> 00:13:09.833
Hi.

200
00:13:10.458 --> 00:13:12.601
I went to Mall Road yesterday.
and I saw something.

201
00:13:12.625 --> 00:13:15.792
And... I thought it'd be perfect for you.

202
00:13:16.402 --> 00:13:17.625
-Rahil.
-No. it's nothing.

203
00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:20.458
But open this only

204
00:13:21.333 --> 00:13:22.333
when you're ready.

205
00:13:23.042 --> 00:13:24.042
For what?

206
00:13:24.917 --> 00:13:30.667
When you're ready to see yourself
through my eyes.

207
00:13:31.292 --> 00:13:32.292
Rahil.

208
00:13:32.667 --> 00:13:34.417
No. seriously. But. please. carry on.

209
00:14:02.708 --> 00:14:04.226
Preeti Kaushik's special sourdough

210
00:14:04.250 --> 00:14:06.976
-with poached eggs and avocado...
-What are you doing? Come here!

211
00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:08.750
-Hey. what happened?
-Come here.

212
00:14:09.292 --> 00:14:10.226
What happened?

213
00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:12.018
You're spoiling me.

214
00:14:12.042 --> 00:14:14.643
The regular customers will think
the owner of this cafe

215
00:14:14.667 --> 00:14:16.417
only pays attention to this girl!

216
00:14:18.417 --> 00:14:21.542
Everyone already knows that
this is the girl

217
00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:24.333
who makes this cafe so special.

218
00:14:27.333 --> 00:14:28.625
Come here.

219
00:14:59.417 --> 00:15:01.726
<i>For days. I've been watching a girl</i>

220
00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:05.250
{\an8}<i>who forgets herself while
taking care of everyone else's hearts.</i>

221
00:15:06.708 --> 00:15:08.500
<i>This little gift is for her</i>

222
00:15:09.250 --> 00:15:14.625
<i>so that when she pauses for a moment.
she can see herself too.</i>

223
00:15:17.083 --> 00:15:19.434
<i>When we meet the right person
at the wrong time.</i>

224
00:15:19.458 --> 00:15:21.708
<i>we tend to blame the timing.</i>

225
00:15:22.333 --> 00:15:24.726
<i>But perhaps the question
isn't about timing at all.</i>

226
00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:26.143
<i>The real question is whether</i>

227
00:15:26.167 --> 00:15:28.167
<i>we were right for ourselves
at that moment.</i>

228
00:15:30.875 --> 00:15:32.726
You're sitting so quietly.

229
00:15:32.750 --> 00:15:34.768
So. what are your hobbies?

230
00:15:34.792 --> 00:15:38.226
Look. all you need to know
about me is that

231
00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:40.125
I absolutely hate my job.

232
00:15:40.792 --> 00:15:42.601
Logistics is such a boring job.

233
00:15:42.625 --> 00:15:46.333
But my mom was telling me
that you're an engineer.

234
00:15:46.958 --> 00:15:49.292
-Yes. I was one in America.
-America!

235
00:15:49.958 --> 00:15:52.583
I've always wanted to settle
in America. honestly!

236
00:15:53.458 --> 00:15:57.667
Now we can settle there
after we get married. right?

237
00:15:58.417 --> 00:15:59.417
No.

238
00:16:00.417 --> 00:16:02.542
Why? You don't like it there?

239
00:16:03.292 --> 00:16:04.268
No.

240
00:16:04.292 --> 00:16:06.059
-What...
-Listen.

241
00:16:06.083 --> 00:16:07.934
-Sudha?
-I need to talk to you for two minutes.

242
00:16:07.958 --> 00:16:11.768
The man sitting with you
is a total scumbag.

243
00:16:11.792 --> 00:16:14.726
-No. no. it's not like that...
-No. don't go by his face.

244
00:16:14.750 --> 00:16:16.268
He's a sex addict.

245
00:16:16.292 --> 00:16:17.268
-Seriously?
-Yes.

246
00:16:17.292 --> 00:16:18.226
What?!

247
00:16:18.250 --> 00:16:20.792
This man only wants
three things from girls.

248
00:16:21.458 --> 00:16:24.226
Lust. lust. and lust.

249
00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:26.393
-No. no. no. she's joking.
-Joking?

250
00:16:26.417 --> 00:16:28.101
-No...
-I'm the one who has become a joke!

251
00:16:28.125 --> 00:16:29.768
-Tell me more.
-You know.

252
00:16:29.792 --> 00:16:32.934
I've narrowly escaped
becoming the mother of his child twice.

253
00:16:32.958 --> 00:16:36.750
-What?!
-For humanity's sake. I can only warn you.

254
00:16:37.292 --> 00:16:40.958
But in the end. it's your life
and your choice. Whatever you decide...

255
00:16:43.125 --> 00:16:44.434
-Yuck!
-No.

256
00:16:44.458 --> 00:16:45.458
Ew!

257
00:16:47.292 --> 00:16:49.167
Boring. my foot!

258
00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:51.750
Mom!

259
00:16:52.750 --> 00:16:53.875
She left.

260
00:16:55.708 --> 00:16:57.542
You're completely crazy. Sudha!

261
00:16:58.333 --> 00:17:00.917
Here's the thing. Chander Mohan Sharma.

262
00:17:01.667 --> 00:17:06.333
You just can't put up with this world
unless you're a little crazy.

263
00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:11.333
Her mom and my aunt are best friends.

264
00:17:11.958 --> 00:17:12.958
Oh.

265
00:17:13.917 --> 00:17:15.792
But you were going to reject her. right?

266
00:17:16.500 --> 00:17:17.917
Convince your aunt too.

267
00:17:19.625 --> 00:17:20.917
How was my acting?

268
00:17:21.458 --> 00:17:22.708
Really terrible.

269
00:17:32.667 --> 00:17:33.958
Oh. man...

270
00:17:37.292 --> 00:17:40.059
Sudha. he's waiting for you.

271
00:17:40.083 --> 00:17:42.768
Kushal! I'm calling you!

272
00:17:42.792 --> 00:17:43.917
Hi.

273
00:17:48.125 --> 00:17:49.208
Bye.

274
00:17:53.875 --> 00:17:56.792
I'll have to go tell poor Kushal Pandit

275
00:17:57.333 --> 00:18:00.042
that you're the father of my future kids.

276
00:18:05.292 --> 00:18:07.125
Do you want to catch a play tomorrow?

277
00:18:08.417 --> 00:18:10.208
-Tomorrow is Monday.
-So?

278
00:18:11.167 --> 00:18:13.167
Do you live less on Mondays?

279
00:18:16.250 --> 00:18:17.250
Bye.

280
00:19:05.333 --> 00:19:06.333
Hi.

281
00:19:07.208 --> 00:19:08.208
Wow.

282
00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:12.667
I mean. you're so...

283
00:19:13.708 --> 00:19:14.875
So...?

284
00:19:18.167 --> 00:19:19.792
You're so on time.

285
00:19:22.708 --> 00:19:26.292
So. shall we go watch
someone else's story in the dark?

286
00:19:29.125 --> 00:19:30.167
Let's go.

287
00:19:31.042 --> 00:19:32.083
Let's.

288
00:19:34.167 --> 00:19:38.101
So back then. from Delhi to my grandma's

289
00:19:38.125 --> 00:19:39.375
and straight back.

290
00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:41.333
We never saw any of this.

291
00:19:43.333 --> 00:19:45.684
Funny how. as children.

292
00:19:45.708 --> 00:19:48.583
we find so much happiness
in the simplest routines.

293
00:19:51.333 --> 00:19:55.059
Anyway. Grandma passed away 20 years ago.

294
00:19:55.083 --> 00:19:57.143
After that. her house was gone.

295
00:19:57.167 --> 00:19:59.708
Gradually. we just stopped coming here.

296
00:20:01.125 --> 00:20:03.625
Now I get why you chose Bhopal.

297
00:20:05.125 --> 00:20:06.125
Why?

298
00:20:07.292 --> 00:20:11.208
"No matter what happens in life.
you should never forget your roots."

299
00:20:13.891 --> 00:20:15.458
Yeah. that's true.

300
00:20:18.167 --> 00:20:19.833
You love Bhopal so much.

301
00:20:20.750 --> 00:20:22.059
Do you want to settle here?

302
00:20:22.083 --> 00:20:23.083
No.

303
00:20:23.833 --> 00:20:24.833
Then where?

304
00:20:26.625 --> 00:20:29.583
-Have you ever been to Bombay?
-I've been to Mumbai.

305
00:20:31.375 --> 00:20:35.875
So. when my dad passed away.
I was in the tenth grade.

306
00:20:37.333 --> 00:20:39.500
He was a lawyer here
at the Bhopal District Court.

307
00:20:40.250 --> 00:20:42.083
His dream was the Bombay High Court.

308
00:20:43.958 --> 00:20:45.542
And now that's your dream.

309
00:20:46.250 --> 00:20:47.976
Just a little bigger than his.

310
00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:49.833
I'm going to start my own law firm.

311
00:20:50.333 --> 00:20:51.375
In Mumbai!

312
00:20:52.667 --> 00:20:56.000
And I'll give Mom
all the happiness she never had.

313
00:20:58.000 --> 00:21:00.667
You know. my dad promised us

314
00:21:01.417 --> 00:21:03.292
that we'd have our own house.

315
00:21:03.792 --> 00:21:05.250
Far from Ratlam.

316
00:21:05.833 --> 00:21:07.917
away from joint family complications.

317
00:21:08.875 --> 00:21:10.833
where it would just be the three of us.

318
00:21:11.625 --> 00:21:13.083
Then he passed away.

319
00:21:14.167 --> 00:21:16.542
And my mom's full attention shifted to me.

320
00:21:18.125 --> 00:21:19.708
She educated me.

321
00:21:20.417 --> 00:21:22.833
gave me the confidence to be independent.

322
00:21:23.542 --> 00:21:25.083
I'm sure she's wonderful.

323
00:21:28.375 --> 00:21:30.851
Yeah. She is.

324
00:21:30.875 --> 00:21:32.542
I can see that.

325
00:21:35.833 --> 00:21:40.000
So yeah. now I'm going to fulfil
both my dreams and my mom's.

326
00:21:41.750 --> 00:21:46.708
Anyway. society doesn't expect girls
to look after their mothers.

327
00:21:49.083 --> 00:21:51.042
We're just given permission. right?

328
00:21:52.458 --> 00:21:53.583
Ouch.

329
00:21:54.583 --> 00:21:56.708
That's why. right now.

330
00:21:57.542 --> 00:22:00.976
I neither have the time

331
00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:04.042
-nor the interest for marriage. and...
-I understand.

332
00:22:20.667 --> 00:22:21.792
Wow.

333
00:22:26.708 --> 00:22:28.625
Thank you for a memorable Monday.

334
00:22:35.208 --> 00:22:36.542
Look. Chander.

335
00:22:37.167 --> 00:22:39.333
If we keep meeting like this.
you'll fall in love.

336
00:22:40.833 --> 00:22:42.500
Maybe I will too.

337
00:22:44.333 --> 00:22:46.917
And if you keep seeing me.

338
00:22:47.458 --> 00:22:49.167
how will you ever settle down?

339
00:22:53.375 --> 00:22:54.351
What?

340
00:22:54.375 --> 00:22:57.583
Madam. where did you go off to?

341
00:22:58.333 --> 00:22:59.333
Somewhere...

342
00:23:00.625 --> 00:23:02.958
I probably shouldn't go.

343
00:23:06.083 --> 00:23:07.375
Okay.

344
00:23:08.833 --> 00:23:12.583
So then... we won't go.

345
00:23:14.250 --> 00:23:15.667
Promise.

346
00:23:34.583 --> 00:23:35.667
Oh!

347
00:24:05.125 --> 00:24:06.417
The moment has passed.

348
00:24:27.583 --> 00:24:28.583
Hello?

349
00:24:30.583 --> 00:24:31.625
Sudha?

350
00:24:35.667 --> 00:24:36.917
So late at night?

351
00:24:38.917 --> 00:24:39.917
Right now?

352
00:24:41.542 --> 00:24:43.500
No. no. I'm coming. I'm coming.

353
00:24:59.958 --> 00:25:01.500
{\an8}HAVE YOU LEFT?

354
00:25:21.208 --> 00:25:22.208
Hey!

355
00:25:23.417 --> 00:25:25.143
What happened? I thought you...

356
00:25:25.167 --> 00:25:26.708
I hate Gargi!

357
00:25:34.250 --> 00:25:36.684
<i>Bhaiya.</i> could you help out a bit?

358
00:25:36.708 --> 00:25:37.708
Sure.

359
00:25:38.583 --> 00:25:40.476
-Keep this one.
-What was the fight about?

360
00:25:40.500 --> 00:25:42.667
Man. what a cliché question to ask!

361
00:25:43.208 --> 00:25:45.059
Do you need a reason to fight?

362
00:25:45.083 --> 00:25:47.708
But there must have been something.

363
00:25:50.417 --> 00:25:52.708
A cold war had been going on for days.

364
00:25:53.583 --> 00:25:56.351
Today. the swearing went a bit too far...

365
00:25:56.375 --> 00:25:57.667
Swearing!

366
00:26:00.583 --> 00:26:01.708
Why are you laughing?

367
00:26:02.500 --> 00:26:03.500
Let's go.

368
00:26:06.458 --> 00:26:07.458
Come on!

369
00:26:11.125 --> 00:26:12.684
Where are we going?

370
00:26:12.708 --> 00:26:15.000
Back to where you just came from.
His place.

371
00:26:17.000 --> 00:26:18.000
Okay.

372
00:26:19.583 --> 00:26:22.042
Is there a movie playing here?
Turn it off!

373
00:26:23.708 --> 00:26:24.792
Okay.

374
00:29:10.125 --> 00:29:12.125
Subtitle translation by: Neha Nair

374
00:29:13.305 --> 00:30:13.291
Do you want subtitles for any video?
